    "findings": [
      {
        "severity": "major",
        "area": "signature",
        "summary": "The stickers exist now across all apps: a ring around each front-page hero, one object per header band, and one vignette per card and figure. They are original and on-topic, but they still don't have the reference's scale and heft. Hero objects are mostly 100–150px on desktop and about 100px on phones. Most show a side band only a few px deep, a sliver about 5% of their height, so they read as flat outlines with a lip. Several band stickers (the overview parcel, the about-page notepad) are pushed into a top corner with half the object off-screen, so they read as fragments. The reference's coins are 200–260px thick die-cut objects with a deep solid rim. They are mostly visible where cropped, and they weigh against the headline to hold the composition.",
        "samples": 1,
        "of": 1,
        "specCaused": false,
        "evidence": [
          "showcase/runs/felt-tip-market/0.1.0-rc.2/review-1/crops/blog--page--home--desktop-light--s1.png",
          "showcase/runs/felt-tip-market/0.1.0-rc.2/review-1/crops/commerce--page--home--desktop-light--s1.png",
          "showcase/runs/felt-tip-market/0.1.0-rc.2/review-1/crops/dashboard--page--home--desktop-light--s1.png",
          "showcase/runs/felt-tip-market/0.1.0-rc.2/review-1/crops/blog--page--about--desktop-light--s1.png",
          "showcase/runs/felt-tip-market/0.1.0-rc.2/dashboard/20261025-025002/drawings/projects-d1.png",
          "showcase/runs/felt-tip-market/0.1.0-rc.2/blog/20261025-025002/drawings/home-d2.png",
          "pipeline/gumroad-study/reference/set/01-desktop.png",
          "pipeline/gumroad-study/reference/set/02-desktop.png"
        ],
        "promptFix": "Before you finish, measure every sticker as it renders. On a desktop hero, at least half the stickers are 180–260px across, and none is under 120px. On a phone, the largest are at least 120px. A header-band sticker is at least as tall as the band's title block plus lead, and at least 60% of it stays visible. Crop it on one edge only, never into a corner where half of it is gone. On every sticker, the side band between the face and the back is a solid strip of the same fill at least 10% of the object's height (about 18px on a 180px object). If a sticker reads as a flat outline with a sliver under it, push the back lower and enlarge the object. Card and figure vignettes use the same depth.",
        "items": [
          "blog--drawings--home",
          "blog--drawings--posts-shipping-a-design-system",
          "blog--drawings--posts-release-notes-people-read",
